keywords: dis, Instruction, Bytecode, Positions, get_instructions, jump_target, label, cache_info, show_caches, hasjump, hasexc
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## dis.Instruction fields (3.14 / current)
  All fields of the Instruction namedtuple/class:

  opcode        int   — Numeric code for operation
  opname        str   — Human readable name for operation
  baseopcode    int   — Numeric code for base operation if specialized; else equals opcode
                        [NEW in 3.13]
  baseopname    str   — Human readable name for base operation if specialized; else equals opname
                        [NEW in 3.13]
  arg           int|None — Numeric argument to operation (if any), otherwise None
  oparg         int|None — Alias for arg [NEW in 3.13]
  argval        Any   — Resolved arg value (if any), otherwise None
  argrepr       str   — Human readable description of operation argument, or empty string
  offset        int   — Start index of operation within bytecode sequence
  start_offset  int   — Start index including prefixed EXTENDED_ARG operations; otherwise equals offset
                        [NEW in 3.13]
  cache_offset  int   — Start index of cache entries following the operation [NEW in 3.13]
  end_offset    int   — End index of cache entries following the operation [NEW in 3.13]
  starts_line   bool  — True if this opcode starts a source line, otherwise False
                        [CHANGED in 3.13: was int|None (line number or None) in 3.12, now bool]
  line_number   int|None — Source line number associated with this opcode (if any) [NEW in 3.13]
  is_jump_target bool — True if other code jumps to here, otherwise False
  jump_target   int|None — Bytecode index of jump target if this is a jump operation, otherwise None
                           [NEW in 3.13]
  positions     dis.Positions — Object holding start and end source locations [NEW in 3.11]
  cache_info    tuple|None — Cache entry information as (name, size, data) triplets; None if no caches
                             [NEW in 3.13]

  CRITICAL GOTCHA for cross-version code:
    Python 3.12:  starts_line = int|None (the line number that starts here, or None)
    Python 3.13+: starts_line = bool (True/False)
    Python 3.13+: line_number = int|None (replaces the old starts_line semantics)
    Python 3.12:  NO jump_target field — must compute from argval or offset arithmetic
    Python 3.13+: jump_target = int|None (byte offset of jump target, or None if not a jump)

  ## dis.Positions class (added 3.11)
  Fields (all may be None if information unavailable):
    lineno         int|None
    end_lineno     int|None
    col_offset     int|None
    end_col_offset int|None

  ## dis.Bytecode class

  Constructor (3.14):
    dis.Bytecode(x, *, first_line=None, current_offset=None,
                 show_caches=False, adaptive=False,
                 show_offsets=False,    # added 3.13
                 show_positions=False)  # added 3.14

  Constructor (3.13):
    dis.Bytecode(x, *, first_line=None, current_offset=None,
                 show_caches=False, adaptive=False,
                 show_offsets=False)

  Constructor (3.12):
    dis.Bytecode(x, *, first_line=None, current_offset=None,
                 show_caches=False, adaptive=False)

  Attributes:
    codeobj    — The compiled code object
    first_line — The first source line of the code object (if available)

  Methods:
    dis()                        — Return formatted bytecode as multi-line string
    info()                       — Return formatted multi-line code object info
    from_traceback(tb, ...)      — Classmethod; constructs from traceback

  ## dis.get_instructions() signature

  3.12:
    dis.get_instructions(x, *, first_line=None, show_caches=False, adaptive=False)
    Returns: Iterator[Instruction]
    Note: show_caches=True emits separate CACHE pseudo-instruction entries

  3.13+:
    dis.get_instructions(x, *, first_line=None, show_caches=False, adaptive=False)
    Note: show_caches parameter DEPRECATED (no effect); cache info always in Instruction.cache_info
    No longer generates separate items for cache entries.

  ## Opcode collections relevant to CFG construction

  dis.hasjump   — Sequence of bytecodes that have a jump target. All jumps are relative.
                  [NEW in 3.13]
  dis.hasexc    — Sequence of bytecodes that set an exception handler [NEW in 3.12]
  dis.hasarg    — Sequence of bytecodes that use their argument [NEW in 3.12]
  dis.hasjrel   — DEPRECATED since 3.13 (all jumps are relative; use hasjump)
  dis.hasjabs   — DEPRECATED since 3.13 (now empty list)

  ## CACHE entries and offset arithmetic

  3.11+: CACHE opcode marks extra space for interpreter inline caches.
  3.12+: Jump argument is target instruction offset RELATIVE to instruction after CACHE entries.
         "CACHE instruction presence is transparent for forward jumps"
  3.13+: get_instructions() no longer emits separate CACHE Instruction items; use cache_info field.
         Cache entries no longer affect jump offset calculations visible to Python-level iteration.

  ## Jump target computation (block leaders)

  3.12: is_jump_target=True on an Instruction means other code jumps to it.
        No explicit jump_target field; compute from: argval (often resolved) or manual offset arithmetic.

  3.13+: instr.jump_target = int offset of jump destination (or None).
         instr.is_jump_target = bool (backward compat preserved).
         Logical labels shown in dis output instead of raw offsets.

  ## Command-line options
  3.13: python -m dis [-C] [-O] file   (-C=show-caches, -O=show-offsets)
  3.14: python -m dis [-C] [-O] [-P] [-S] file  (-P=show-positions, -S=specialized)

  ## Version history summary for dis.Instruction
  3.4:  initial (opcode, opname, arg, argval, argrepr, offset, starts_line, is_jump_target)
  3.11: positions field added
  3.13: start_offset, cache_offset, end_offset, baseopname, baseopcode, jump_target,
        oparg, line_number, cache_info added; starts_line changed bool; show_caches deprecated
  3.14: show_positions added to Bytecode/dis()/disassemble()
<<<END>>>

