id: 8
ts: 2026-05-28T00:08:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: Python 3.14 What's New — bytecode/opcode changes
authors: Python core developers
year: 2025
venue: docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.14.html
quality: DOCS
url: https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.14.html
keywords: RETURN_CONST removed, BEFORE_WITH removed, LOAD_SMALL_INT, LOAD_FAST_BORROW, LOAD_SPECIAL, POP_ITER, NOT_TAKEN, BUILD_TEMPLATE, BUILD_INTERPOLATION, BINARY_SUBSCR removed, show_positions
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## Python 3.14 opcode changes (confirmed from docs + issue #135447)

  REMOVED in 3.14:
    RETURN_CONST        — removed (gh-125837, Mark Shannon)
                          Was in 3.12 and 3.13. Now use LOAD_CONST/LOAD_SMALL_INT + RETURN_VALUE.
    BEFORE_WITH         — removed
    BEFORE_ASYNC_WITH   — removed
                          Replaced by LOAD_SPECIAL instruction.
    BINARY_SUBSCR       — removed (per gh-135447 issue report)

  ADDED in 3.14:
    LOAD_SMALL_INT(i)   — pushes small integer equal to oparg i to the stack
                          (replaces part of what LOAD_CONST + RETURN_CONST did)
    LOAD_FAST_BORROW    — reduced reference-counting for local vars where frame outlives ref
    LOAD_FAST_BORROW_LOAD_FAST_BORROW — optimized variant
    LOAD_SPECIAL(namei) — special method lookup; for with/async-with
                          If type(STACK[-1]).__xxx__ is a method: push (method, self)
                          If not a method: push (value, NULL)
                          namei encodes which special method via dedicated enum
    POP_ITER            — removes iterator from top of stack; added 3.14
    NOT_TAKEN           — branch prediction hint (undocumented per gh-135447)
    BUILD_TEMPLATE      — for f-string template construction (undocumented per gh-135447)
    BUILD_INTERPOLATION — for f-string interpolation (undocumented per gh-135447)
    LOAD_COMMON_CONSTANT — loads commonly-used constants

  DOCUMENTATION GAPS (per github.com/python/cpython/issues/135447):
    NOT_TAKEN, POP_ITER, BUILD_TEMPLATE, BUILD_INTERPOLATION missing from dis docs
    as of issue filing. PRs #135478, #135803, #139399 filed to fix.
    Changes after 3.14a2 (magic number 3609) were underdocumented.

  ## dis module changes in 3.14
    show_positions parameter added to: dis.Bytecode, dis.dis(), dis.distb(),
      dis.disassemble(), dis.disco()
    --show-positions / -P command-line flag added
    --specialized / -S command-line flag added

  ## With-statement in 3.14

  BEFORE_WITH removed; LOAD_SPECIAL replaces it.
  Pattern for `with ctx as x:` in 3.14:
    LOAD_SPECIAL  (loads __enter__ method)
    CALL          (calls __enter__, result bound to x)
    ... body ...
    LOAD_SPECIAL  (loads __exit__ method — implicitly covered by exception table entry)
    (exception path) WITH_EXCEPT_START → POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE → RERAISE

  Exact oparg encoding for LOAD_SPECIAL: uses dedicated enum for __enter__/__exit__ etc.

  ## CFG terminator opcode list for 3.14

  Unconditional terminators (no fallthrough):
    RETURN_VALUE
    RAISE_VARARGS
    RERAISE
    JUMP_FORWARD
    JUMP_BACKWARD
    JUMP_BACKWARD_NO_INTERRUPT

  Conditional terminators (two successors):
    POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE
    POP_JUMP_IF_FALSE
    POP_JUMP_IF_NONE
    POP_JUMP_IF_NOT_NONE
    FOR_ITER
    SEND

  NOT a terminator (despite being for context managers):
    LOAD_SPECIAL (just sets up for __enter__/__exit__ call)
    WITH_EXCEPT_START (only in exception handler path)
<<<END>>>

