title: PEP 657 — Fine-Grained Error Locations (co_positions API)
authors: Pablo Galindo Salgado, Batuhan Taskaya, et al.
year: 2021
venue: peps.python.org/pep-0657/
quality: SPEC
url: https://peps.python.org/pep-0657/
keywords: co_positions, fine-grained error locations, column offsets, end_lineno, end_col_offset, PyCode_Addr2Location, co_linetable
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## co_positions() Python API (added 3.11)

  code.co_positions()
  Returns: iterator of (start_line, end_line, start_column, end_column) tuples
  One tuple per instruction (including CACHE pseudo-instructions).
  Values may be None if position information not available for that instruction.
  Note from PEP: offsets > 255 treated as missing (return -1 from C API, None from Python API).

  ## PyCode_Addr2Location (C API added 3.11)

  int PyCode_Addr2Location(PyObject *co, int byte_offset,
                            int *start_line, int *start_column,
                            int *end_line, int *end_column)
  Sets to 0 (not None) when information unavailable.
  Returns: 1 on success, 0 on failure.

  ## dis.Positions namedtuple (added 3.11)

  Positions(lineno, end_lineno, col_offset, end_col_offset)
  All fields int|None.
  Populated from co_positions() iterator.
  Available on Instruction.positions field.

  ## Semantics

  Fine-grained: gives precise source span for each bytecode instruction.
  Useful for tools that need to highlight exact source text responsible for each op.
  For pflow: can map each CFG node/edge to source span for diagnostics.

  ## Storage

  Stored in co_linetable (same field, but with extended format encoding position info).
  co_linetable format extended in 3.11 to include column info (entry types 0-15).
  Prior to 3.11: co_lnotab stored only line numbers, 2 bytes per entry.
<<<END>>>


