cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## Numeric opcode values in Python 3.12.0

  Exception & control flow (numeric values):
    PUSH_EXC_INFO              = 35
    CHECK_EXC_MATCH            = 36
    WITH_EXCEPT_START          = 49
    BEFORE_WITH                = 53   ← exists in 3.12
    POP_EXCEPT                 = 89
    RERAISE                    = 119
    RETURN_CONST               = 121  ← added in 3.12
    JUMP_FORWARD               = 110  (jrel_op)
    JUMP_BACKWARD              = 140  (jrel_op)
    JUMP_BACKWARD_NO_INTERRUPT = 134  (jrel_op)
    FOR_ITER                   = 93   (jrel_op)
    SEND                       = 123  (jrel_op)
    RAISE_VARARGS              = 130
    EXTENDED_ARG               = 144

  ## hasjrel in 3.12 (relative jumps — NOT yet deprecated)
    FOR_ITER (93)
    JUMP_FORWARD (110)
    POP_JUMP_IF_FALSE (114)
    POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE (115)
    POP_JUMP_IF_NOT_NONE (128)
    POP_JUMP_IF_NONE (129)
    JUMP_BACKWARD_NO_INTERRUPT (134)
    JUMP_BACKWARD (140)
    SEND (123)

  ## hasexc in 3.12 (pseudo-instructions: set exception handler)
    SETUP_FINALLY (256)
    SETUP_CLEANUP (257)
    SETUP_WITH    (258)

  ## hasarg in 3.12
    All opcodes >= 90 (HAVE_ARGUMENT threshold) use their argument.

  ## HAVE_ARGUMENT threshold
    = 90 in 3.12
    Real opcodes < 90: no argument (e.g., PUSH_EXC_INFO=35 has no oparg)
    Real opcodes >= 90: have argument (e.g., JUMP_FORWARD=110 has delta)

  ## BEFORE_WITH semantics in 3.12/3.13
    BEFORE_WITH: sets up with-statement.
    Loads __exit__ method and pushes to stack position, then calls __enter__.
    oparg = 1: push lasti (preserve instruction offset for exception handler)
    Used by WITH_EXCEPT_START in the exception handler path.
    The with-body is protected by an exception table entry.
    Exception handler entry: target = PUSH_EXC_INFO instruction.
    Handler body: PUSH_EXC_INFO, WITH_EXCEPT_START, POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE, RERAISE.

  ## WITH_EXCEPT_START semantics (all versions 3.12-3.14)
    Calls __exit__(exc_type, exc_val, exc_tb).
    __exit__ is at stack position 4 (in 3.11+, was 7 in 3.10).
    Result used by POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE: if truthy, exception suppressed (jump to cleanup).
    If falsy, RERAISE re-raises the exception.
    NOT a basic-block terminator.
<<<END>>>

