id: 19
ts: 2026-05-28T00:19:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: BEFORE_WITH removal in 3.14 and LOAD_SPECIAL replacement — with-statement bytecode patterns
authors: Python core developers
year: 2025
venue: github.com + docs.python.org
quality: DOCS
url: https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.14.html
keywords: BEFORE_WITH removed 3.14, LOAD_SPECIAL, with statement 3.14 bytecode, WITH_EXCEPT_START still present
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## BEFORE_WITH and BEFORE_ASYNC_WITH removal in 3.14

  BEFORE_WITH and BEFORE_ASYNC_WITH removed in Python 3.14.
  Replaced by LOAD_SPECIAL instruction.

  In 3.12/3.13 pattern for `with ctx as x:`:
    BEFORE_WITH        (loads __exit__, calls __enter__, pushes result)
    <store result to x>
    <body>
    ... (exception table entry covers body → exception handler)
    Exception handler: PUSH_EXC_INFO → WITH_EXCEPT_START → POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE → RERAISE

  In 3.14 pattern for `with ctx as x:`:
    LOAD_SPECIAL(n)   (loads __enter__ special method; n = enum for __enter__)
    CALL              (calls __enter__, pushes result)
    <store result to x>
    <body>
    ... (exception table entry covers body → exception handler)
    Exception handler path:
      LOAD_SPECIAL(m)  (loads __exit__ method; m = enum for __exit__)
      WITH_EXCEPT_START (still present in 3.14 — calls __exit__ with exc info)
      POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE  (suppress or reraise)
      RERAISE

  ## WITH_EXCEPT_START still present in 3.14
  WITH_EXCEPT_START is NOT removed in 3.14.
  It remains as the instruction that calls __exit__ in the exception handler path.

  ## LOAD_SPECIAL oparg encoding
  oparg encodes which special method to load using a dedicated enum.
  Specific enum values not documented in public docs as of this research.
  Applies to: __enter__, __exit__, __aenter__, __aexit__, and potentially others.

  ## pflow CFG implications

  For version-gated with-statement handling:

  3.12/3.13: BEFORE_WITH instruction in bytecode stream.
    - is_jump_target=False (not a block leader itself)
    - Exception table entry covers bytecode from after BEFORE_WITH through end of body
    - Exception handler block starts with PUSH_EXC_INFO (block leader via exception table target)

  3.14: No BEFORE_WITH. LOAD_SPECIAL instead.
    - Exception table entry still covers body
    - Exception handler block still starts with PUSH_EXC_INFO (or equivalent)
    - WITH_EXCEPT_START still in exception handler path

  ## Identifying with-statement exception edges
  In all versions 3.12-3.14:
    Exception table entry with target pointing to a block starting with PUSH_EXC_INFO,
    followed by WITH_EXCEPT_START → indicates with-statement exception cleanup.
    Distinguished from try/except by: WITH_EXCEPT_START (not CHECK_EXC_MATCH).
<<<END>>>


SOURCE
id: 20
ts: 2026-05-28T00:20:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: Python 3.14 dis.rst — complete instruction reference for new 3.14 opcodes
authors: Python core developers
year: 2025
venue: raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/main/Doc/library/dis.rst
quality: DOCS
url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/main/Doc/library/dis.rst
keywords: NOT_TAKEN, POP_ITER, LOAD_SPECIAL, BUILD_TEMPLATE, BUILD_INTERPOLATION, WITH_EXCEPT_START, PUSH_EXC_INFO, CHECK_EXC_MATCH, RERAISE, RAISE_VARARGS, JUMP_FORWARD, JUMP_BACKWARD, FOR_ITER, SEND
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## New opcodes in 3.14 (from dis.rst main branch)

  NOT_TAKEN
    No-op code. Used by interpreter to record BRANCH_LEFT and BRANCH_RIGHT events
    for sys.monitoring.
    Added 3.14. NOT a basic-block terminator.
    Implementation: macro(NOT_TAKEN) = NOP (alias to NOP)

  POP_ITER
    Removes iterator from top of stack.
    Stack effect: pops iter, pops index_or_null (two items).
    Added 3.14.
    Implementation:
      inst(POP_ITER, (iter, index_or_null -- )) {
          (void)index_or_null;
          DEAD(index_or_null);
          PyStackRef_CLOSE(iter);
      }

  LOAD_SPECIAL
    Performs special method lookup on STACK[-1].
    If type(STACK[-1]).__xxx__ is a method:
      leaves type(STACK[-1]).__xxx__; STACK[-1] on the stack
    If type(STACK[-1]).__xxx__ is not a method:
      leaves STACK[-1].__xxx__; NULL on the stack
    oparg: encodes which special method using a dedicated enum.
    Added 3.14. Replaces BEFORE_WITH (for with-statements).
    dis output: "LOAD_SPECIAL  1" (numeric, no attribute name yet — see gh-120780)

  BUILD_TEMPLATE
    Constructs a new Template instance from:
      interpolations = STACK.pop()
      strings = STACK.pop()
      STACK.append(_build_template(strings, interpolations))
    Added 3.14.

  BUILD_INTERPOLATION(format)
    Constructs a new Interpolation instance from value and source expression.
    oparg encodes: conversion = format >> 2, has_format_spec = format & 1
    Added 3.14.

  ## RETURN_VALUE (confirmed present in 3.14)
    Returns with STACK[-1] to caller. No change.
    Terminates basic block.

  ## RETURN_CONST (confirmed removed in 3.14)
    Was present in 3.12 and 3.13: return co_consts[consti].
    NOT present in 3.14 dis.rst. Confirmed removed.

  ## BEFORE_WITH (confirmed removed in 3.14)
    NOT present in 3.14 dis.rst. Confirmed removed.
    Replaced by LOAD_SPECIAL.

  ## bytecodes.c confirms (from fetch of main branch)
    RETURN_VALUE: macro(RETURN_VALUE) = _MAKE_HEAP_SAFE + _RETURN_VALUE
    NOT_TAKEN: macro(NOT_TAKEN) = NOP
    POP_ITER: inst(POP_ITER, (iter, index_or_null -- ))
    RETURN_CONST: NOT FOUND in main branch bytecodes.c (confirms removal)
    BEFORE_WITH: NOT FOUND in main branch bytecodes.c (confirms removal)
    LOAD_SPECIAL: NOT in the excerpt fetched (likely in another section of bytecodes.c)

  ## LOAD_SPECIAL oparg values (from gh-120507 and gh-120780)
    Proposed bytecode pattern for `with ctx as x:`:
      COPY 1
      LOAD_SPECIAL __enter__ + NULL|self
      SWAP 3
      LOAD_SPECIAL __exit__
      SWAP 3
      CALL 0
    oparg values: numeric, not yet documented. 
    dis displays "LOAD_SPECIAL 1" without attribute name (tracked in gh-120780).
    From context: 0 = one value (__enter__?), 1 = another (__exit__?).
    PR #120640 implements this change.

  ## WITH_EXCEPT_START (confirmed present in 3.14)
    Calls function at stack position 4 with (type, val, tb).
    Used to call __exit__ in exception handler for with-statement.
    Still present and unchanged semantically from 3.11 form.
    NOT a terminator.

  ## Key exception-related instructions (unchanged across 3.12-3.14)
    PUSH_EXC_INFO: pops, pushes current exception, pushes original. Added 3.11.
    POP_EXCEPT: pops exception state restoration value. Changed 3.11.
    CHECK_EXC_MATCH: tests STACK[-2] isinstance STACK[-1]. Added 3.11.
    RERAISE(lasti): re-raises TOS exception; if lasti non-zero, pops+sets f_lasti.
    RAISE_VARARGS(argc): 0=reraise, 1=raise, 2=raise from.
<<<END>>>

