cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## PR #120640 — "Lower the BEFORE_WITH and BEFORE_ASYNC_WITH instructions"

  Author: Mark Shannon
  Merged into 3.14.

  ## Proposed bytecode pattern for `with ctx as x:` (from issue description)

  COPY 1
  LOAD_SPECIAL __enter__ + NULL|self
  SWAP 3
  LOAD_SPECIAL __exit__
  SWAP 3
  CALL 0

  ## LOAD_SPECIAL description from issue

  "A new LOAD_SPECIAL instruction was introduced to handle loading dunder methods,
   replacing the previous bulky instructions that didn't optimize effectively in tier 2."

  ## LOAD_SPECIAL oparg numeric values

  dis shows numeric oparg only: "LOAD_SPECIAL 1" (no attribute name).
  Issue gh-120780 requests adding attribute name to dis output.
  Follow-up PR #120781 addresses documentation.
  Exact mapping of oparg integer → method name NOT confirmed from available sources.
  From issue context: 0 and 1 are used for __enter__/__exit__ respectively (order uncertain).

  ## Implication for pflow CFG construction in 3.14

  For with-statement detection in 3.14 bytecode:
    Cannot search for BEFORE_WITH (removed).
    Must detect LOAD_SPECIAL + CALL sequence at start of with-body setup.
    Exception handler still uses WITH_EXCEPT_START.
    Exception table entry still covers the with-body.
    Block leader for handler: still PUSH_EXC_INFO.

  ## async-with changes
    BEFORE_ASYNC_WITH also removed in 3.14.
    LOAD_SPECIAL(n) with appropriate enum values for __aenter__/__aexit__.
    WITH_EXCEPT_START equivalent for async also changed accordingly.
<<<END>>>


SOURCE
id: 22
ts: 2026-05-28T00:22:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: PR #120640 — Lower BEFORE_WITH/BEFORE_ASYNC_WITH to LOAD_SPECIAL — exact oparg values
authors: Mark Shannon
year: 2024
venue: github.com/python/cpython/pull/120640
quality: CODE
url: https://github.com/python/cpython/pull/120640
keywords: LOAD_SPECIAL oparg, __enter__=1, __exit__=0, BEFORE_WITH removed, with-statement pattern 3.14
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## LOAD_SPECIAL oparg values (from PR #120640)

  CONFIRMED from PR description:
    LOAD_SPECIAL oparg 0 → loads __exit__ (or __aexit__ for async)
    LOAD_SPECIAL oparg 1 → loads __enter__ (or __aenter__ for async)

  ## Exact bytecode pattern for `with ctx as x:` in 3.14

  COPY                     1      (duplicate ctx reference)
  LOAD_SPECIAL             1      (load __enter__ from ctx)
  SWAP                     2
  SWAP                     3
  LOAD_SPECIAL             0      (load __exit__ from ctx)
  CALL                     0      (call __enter__)
  <store result to x>
  <body>
  ... (exception table entry covers body)
  Exception handler:
    PUSH_EXC_INFO
    WITH_EXCEPT_START  (calls __exit__ with exc_info)
    POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE   (if __exit__ returns truthy: suppress exception)
    RERAISE            (otherwise: propagate exception)

  ## Performance note from PR

  "Negligible performance impact" — the instruction sequence is longer but
  more amenable to tier-2 JIT optimization.
  Exposes _PyObject_LookupSpecialMethod for JIT access.

  ## Stack effect of LOAD_SPECIAL

  If type(obj).__xxx__ is a method:
    Pushes: (method, obj)  ← obj stays on stack, method added above
  If type(obj).__xxx__ is not a method:
    Pushes: (bound_method_or_attr, NULL)  ← NULL placeholder for self

  This mirrors the LOAD_ATTR(method-call) behavior with low bit set.
  Result: stack has two items where CALL expects (callable + self/NULL).
<<<END>>>


