id: 25
ts: 2026-05-28T00:25:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: Python 3.12 dis.py source — Instruction namedtuple (9 fields), findlabels, findlinestarts (verbatim)
authors: Python core developers
year: 2023
venue: raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.12.0/Lib/dis.py
quality: CODE
url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.12.0/Lib/dis.py
keywords: Instruction 3.12 fields, starts_line int OR None, no jump_target, no line_number, findlabels 3.12, findlinestarts 3.12
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## Python 3.12 Instruction namedtuple (verbatim)

  _Instruction = collections.namedtuple(
      "_Instruction",
      [
          'opname',
          'opcode',
          'arg',
          'argval',
          'argrepr',
          'offset',
          'starts_line',
          'is_jump_target',
          'positions'
      ],
      defaults=[None]
  )

  FIELDS IN 3.12 (9 total, NOT class-based):
    opname, opcode, arg, argval, argrepr, offset,
    starts_line (int|None — the line number if this starts a line, else None),
    is_jump_target (bool),
    positions (dis.Positions|None, added 3.11)

  CRITICAL DIFFERENCES from 3.13+:
    - starts_line: int|None in 3.12 (line number value OR None)
    - is_jump_target: stored field in namedtuple (not property)
    - NO start_offset, NO cache_offset, NO end_offset, NO line_number
    - NO jump_target, NO cache_info, NO baseopname, NO baseopcode
    - NO oparg (use arg instead)
    - NO label field

  ## findlabels in Python 3.12 (verbatim)

  def findlabels(code):
      labels = []
      for offset, op, arg in _unpack_opargs(code):
          if arg is not None:
              deop = _deoptop(op)
              caches = _inline_cache_entries[deop]
              if deop in hasjrel:
                  if _is_backward_jump(deop):
                      arg = -arg
                  label = offset + 2 + arg*2
                  label += 2 * caches
              elif deop in hasjabs:
                  label = arg*2
              else:
                  continue
              if label not in labels:
                  labels.append(label)
      return labels

  Note: In 3.12, uses _unpack_opargs(code) yielding (offset, op, arg)
  (vs 3.13+ which yields (offset, start_offset, op, arg))
  Note: deop = _deoptop(op) deoptimizes specialized opcodes to base opcode.
  Note: _inline_cache_entries (not _get_cache_size) in 3.12.

  ## findlinestarts in Python 3.12 (verbatim)

  def findlinestarts(code):
      lastline = None
      for start, end, line in code.co_lines():
          if line is not None and line != lastline:
              lastline = line
              yield start, line
      return

  Note: Slightly different from 3.13+ (which uses lastline=False).
  Key: yields only when line changes AND is not None (skips instructions without line).

  ## _parse_exception_table in Python 3.12 (verbatim — same implementation as 3.13)

  def _parse_exception_table(code):
      iterator = iter(code.co_exceptiontable)
      entries = []
      try:
          while True:
              start = _parse_varint(iterator)*2
              length = _parse_varint(iterator)*2
              end = start + length
              target = _parse_varint(iterator)*2
              dl = _parse_varint(iterator)
              depth = dl >> 1
              lasti = bool(dl&1)
              entries.append(_ExceptionTableEntry(start, end, target, depth, lasti))
      except StopIteration:
          return entries

  Implementation is IDENTICAL to 3.13+ _parse_exception_table.

  ## _parse_varint in Python 3.12 (verbatim — same as 3.13)

  def _parse_varint(iterator):
      b = next(iterator)
      val = b & 63
      while b&64:
          val <<= 6
          b = next(iterator)
          val |= b&63
      return val

  Same implementation as 3.13+.
<<<END>>>

