title: Python 3.14.0 dis.py source (stable release) — _make_labels_map, findlabels (verbatim)
authors: Python core developers
year: 2025
venue: raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.14.0/Lib/dis.py
quality: CODE
url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.14.0/Lib/dis.py
keywords: _make_labels_map, findlabels 3.14, exception_entries inclusion in labels, is_jump_target semantics 3.14
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## _make_labels_map (3.13+ / 3.14.0 stable)

  Creates mapping from byte offset → logical label number.
  Input: (original_code, exception_entries=())
  Returns: dict[int, int]  (offset → label_number, 1-indexed)

  Algorithm:
    labels = set()
    # Add jump targets:
    labels |= set(findlabels(code))
    # Add exception table targets:
    for entry in exception_entries:
        labels.add(entry.target)
    # Assign sequential numbers:
    return {offset: i+1 for i, offset in enumerate(sorted(labels))}

  KEY: Exception handler targets (entry.target) ARE in the labels_map.
  Therefore: instructions at exception handler targets have label set.
  Therefore: their is_jump_target property returns True (since label is not None).

  ## findlabels in 3.14.0 (same as 3.13+)

  Uses _get_jump_target() which handles all relative jumps.
  hasjabs is empty list → only relative jumps processed.
  Returns list of byte offsets that are jump targets.
  Does NOT include exception table targets.
  (Exception table targets added separately in _make_labels_map.)

  ## dis.Instruction in 3.14.0 stable — same as main branch

  Same 12 namedtuple fields + properties as documented in records 5 and 26.
  No additional changes between 3.13 and 3.14 for Instruction fields.

  ## Confirmed 3.14.0 stable features

  show_positions parameter: available in Bytecode.__init__, dis.dis(), etc.
  Instruction.positions: always populated (Positions namedtuple).
  RETURN_CONST: NOT in 3.14.0 opmap (confirmed removed).
  BEFORE_WITH: NOT in 3.14.0 opmap (confirmed removed).
  LOAD_SPECIAL: present in 3.14.0.
  POP_ITER: present in 3.14.0.
  NOT_TAKEN: present in 3.14.0.
<<<END>>>


