title: PyCodeObject structure — co_exceptiontable, co_linetable, co_code_adaptive fields
authors: Python core developers
year: 2026
venue: raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/main/Include/cpython/code.h
quality: CODE
url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/main/Include/cpython/code.h
keywords: PyCodeObject, co_exceptiontable, co_linetable, co_code_adaptive, co_flags, co_firstlineno, co_stacksize, co_version
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## PyCodeObject struct definition (from code.h)

  Constructed via _PyCode_DEF(SIZE) macro. Key fields:

  Hot fields (performance-critical):
    PyObject *co_consts         — list of constants used (co_consts[i] = constant)
    PyObject *co_names          — list of name strings
    PyObject *co_exceptiontable — "Byte string encoding exception handling table"
                                  Type: PyObject* (bytes object)
    int co_flags                — control flags (CO_OPTIMIZED, CO_NEWLOCALS, CO_VARARGS, etc.)

  Core metadata:
    int co_argcount             — positional argument count
    int co_posonlyargcount      — positional-only argument count
    int co_kwonlyargcount       — keyword-only argument count
    int co_stacksize            — evaluation stack size needed
    int co_firstlineno          — "first source line number"
    int co_nlocals              — number of local variables

  Line and location info:
    PyObject *co_linetable      — "bytes object that holds location info"
                                  (co_linetable encodes both line numbers AND column positions)
    char co_code_adaptive[(SIZE)] — adaptive bytecode array (not co_code in 3.11+)

  Version tracking:
    uint32_t co_version
    uintptr_t _co_instrumentation_version

  ## co_exceptiontable access from Python

  Python: code.co_exceptiontable  (bytes object)
  Parsed by: dis._parse_exception_table(code) → list of _ExceptionTableEntry

  ## co_linetable access from Python

  Python: code.co_linetable  (bytes object, encoding is opaque/version-dependent)
  API: code.co_lines()       → iterator of (start, end, line) tuples
       code.co_positions()   → iterator of (lineno, end_lineno, col_offset, end_col_offset) tuples

  ## co_code in 3.11+

  In 3.11+: code.co_code returns bytes (recreated from co_code_adaptive).
  The underlying storage is co_code_adaptive (mutable array in the struct).
  co_code is a read-only property producing a bytes copy.

  ## IS_TERMINATOR_OPCODE usage (from assemble.c)

  Macro IS_TERMINATOR_OPCODE is USED in assemble.c:
    if (IS_TERMINATOR_OPCODE(instr->i_opcode)) {
        instr->i_loc = NO_LOCATION;
    }
  But defined in: pycore_opcode_metadata.h (included by assemble.c).
  Could not extract exact definition from available sources.
  From context: covers RETURN_VALUE, RERAISE, RAISE_VARARGS, JUMP_FORWARD,
                JUMP_BACKWARD, JUMP_BACKWARD_NO_INTERRUPT, RETURN_CONST (3.12/3.13).
  Essentially: IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE ∪ IS_UNCONDITIONAL_JUMP_OPCODE.
<<<END>>>

