id: 34
ts: 2026-05-28T00:34:00Z
relevance: HIGH
title: LOAD_SMALL_INT opcode — Python 3.14 small integer optimization
authors: Python core developers
year: 2025
venue: docs.python.org/3/library/dis.html + github.com/python/cpython/issues/140256
quality: DOCS
url: https://docs.python.org/3/library/dis.html
keywords: LOAD_SMALL_INT, small integer, oparg=integer value, co_consts replacement, 3.14 optimization
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## LOAD_SMALL_INT (Python 3.14)

  Opcode: LOAD_SMALL_INT(i)
  Stack effect: pushes integer value equal to oparg i onto stack.
  oparg: the integer value itself (NOT an index into co_consts).
  Range: "small integers" — exact range not documented but implied by name (likely -5 to 256 or similar).

  Purpose: Replaces LOAD_CONST for commonly-used small integer literals.
  Avoids storing small integers in co_consts table.
  oparg IS the value, not a reference to co_consts.

  NOT a basic-block terminator.
  Added 3.14.

  Known issue (gh-140256): LOAD_SMALL_INT has empty argrepr via Bytecode
    (dis doesn't show the integer value in argrepr by default — display bug, not semantic issue).

  ## LOAD_COMMON_CONSTANT (Python 3.14)

  Loads commonly-used constants (presumably None, True, False, etc.) directly.
  oparg encodes which constant via dedicated enum.
  Similar to LOAD_SMALL_INT but for non-integer constants.
  NOT a basic-block terminator.

  ## pflow implication

  In 3.14, RETURN_CONST is removed. Small integer returns become:
    LOAD_SMALL_INT  <value>
    RETURN_VALUE
  Regular constant returns:
    LOAD_CONST   <consti>
    RETURN_VALUE
  None return (implicit): 
    LOAD_COMMON_CONSTANT  <None enum>
    RETURN_VALUE
  (or possibly LOAD_CONST   None  depending on optimizer decisions)
<<<END>>>


