  ## IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE in Python 3.12.0 (verbatim)

  #define IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE(opcode) \
          ((opcode) == RETURN_VALUE || \
           (opcode) == RETURN_CONST || \    ← PRESENT in 3.12!
           (opcode) == RAISE_VARARGS || \
           (opcode) == RERAISE)

  KEY FINDING: RETURN_CONST IS included in IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE for Python 3.12.
  This confirms RETURN_CONST terminates a basic block in 3.12.

  ## IS_TERMINATOR_OPCODE in Python 3.12.0 (verbatim)

  #define IS_TERMINATOR_OPCODE(opcode) \
          (IS_JUMP_OPCODE(opcode) || IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE(opcode))

  Note: 3.12 uses IS_JUMP_OPCODE (not OPCODE_HAS_JUMP as in main branch).

  ## IS_UNCONDITIONAL_JUMP_OPCODE in Python 3.12.0 (verbatim)

  #define IS_UNCONDITIONAL_JUMP_OPCODE(opcode) \
          ((opcode) == JUMP || \
           (opcode) == JUMP_NO_INTERRUPT || \
           (opcode) == JUMP_FORWARD || \
           (opcode) == JUMP_BACKWARD || \
           (opcode) == JUMP_BACKWARD_NO_INTERRUPT)

  Same as main branch.

  ## Missing in 3.12

  IS_CONDITIONAL_JUMP_OPCODE — not present in 3.12.0 version.
  (Added later or in different file in 3.12 release.)

  ## Complete IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE by version

  Python 3.12-3.13:
    IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE = RETURN_VALUE | RETURN_CONST | RAISE_VARARGS | RERAISE

  Python 3.14+:
    IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE = RETURN_VALUE | RAISE_VARARGS | RERAISE
    (RETURN_CONST removed from both the opcode set AND from IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE)

  ## Complete IS_UNCONDITIONAL_JUMP_OPCODE (all versions 3.12-3.14)

  Final bytecode terminators (JUMP and JUMP_NO_INTERRUPT are pseudo; never in dis output):
    JUMP_FORWARD
    JUMP_BACKWARD
    JUMP_BACKWARD_NO_INTERRUPT
<<<END>>>

