id: 37
ts: 2026-05-28T00:37:00Z
relevance: MED
title: Python .pyc magic numbers for 3.12, 3.13, 3.14
authors: Python core developers
year: 2025
venue: raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/main/Include/internal/pycore_magic_number.h
quality: CODE
url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/main/Include/internal/pycore_magic_number.h
keywords: magic number, pyc format, Python 3.12 3518, Python 3.13 3571, Python 3.14 3627, pyc version identification
cites:
cited_by:
content:
  ## Magic number formula (3.11+)
  Base = 2900 + 50 * minor_version
  Python 3.12 base: 2900 + 50*12 = 3500
  Python 3.13 base: 2900 + 50*13 = 3550
  Python 3.14 base: 2900 + 50*14 = 3600

  Incremented by 1 for each file format change within a minor version.

  ## Python 3.12 magic number range: 3500-3531
  Notable: 3518 = Add RETURN_CONST instruction
  Final 3.12 stable release: 3531

  ## Python 3.13 magic number range: 3550-3571
  Notable: 3550 = Plugin optimizer support
  Final 3.13 stable: ~3571

  ## Python 3.14 magic number range: 3600-3627
  Notable:
    3600-3608: LOAD_COMMON_CONSTANT, LOAD_SPECIAL, slice changes
    3609: Add LOAD_SMALL_INT, LOAD_CONST_IMMORTAL, remove RETURN_CONST
    3610-3613: POP_ITER and other additions
    3614-3627: binary ops, async monitoring, annotation fixes
  As of 3.14.0rc2: magic number changed (discussion.python.org post)

  ## .pyc file format
  First 4 bytes of .pyc file:
    bytes 0-1: magic number (uint16, little-endian)
    bytes 2-3: '\r\n' (CR LF, prevents accidental text-mode corruption)
  Then: flags (4 bytes), source mtime (4 bytes), source size (4 bytes), code object.

  ## Relevance to pflow

  To identify Python version from a .pyc file:
    magic = struct.unpack('<H', data[0:2])[0]
    if 3500 <= magic <= 3531: version = (3, 12)
    elif 3550 <= magic <= 3571: version = (3, 13)
    elif 3600 <= magic: version = (3, 14)  # approximate

  NOTE: This is an approximate version gate; actual checks should use sys.version_info.
<<<END>>>


