  IS_SCOPE_EXIT_OPCODE:
    3.12.0: {RETURN_VALUE, RETURN_CONST, RAISE_VARARGS, RERAISE}
    3.14:   {RETURN_VALUE, RAISE_VARARGS, RERAISE}

  IS_TERMINATOR_OPCODE inner predicate:
    3.12.0: IS_JUMP_OPCODE (bit table lookup)
    3.14:   OPCODE_HAS_JUMP (different name, possibly same semantics)

  IS_CONDITIONAL_JUMP_OPCODE:
    3.12.0: NOT FOUND (may be absent or defined elsewhere)
    3.14:   {POP_JUMP_IF_FALSE, POP_JUMP_IF_TRUE, POP_JUMP_IF_NONE, POP_JUMP_IF_NOT_NONE}

  ## Note on dis.Bytecode.exception_entries

  From Bytecode.__init__:
    self.exception_entries = _parse_exception_table(co)
  This is an INSTANCE ATTRIBUTE, not documented in official docs but accessible.
  Returns list[_ExceptionTableEntry].
  Available in ALL versions 3.12-3.14 (since Bytecode.__init__ always sets it).
  Useful for pflow to access exception table without calling the private function directly:
    bytecode = dis.Bytecode(func)
    exc_entries = bytecode.exception_entries
    # Returns list[_ExceptionTableEntry(start, end, target, depth, lasti)]
<<<END>>>

